  "bio": "First elected at 29 years old, Representative Trey Martinez Fischer is currently serving his 12th legislative session fighting for the people of San Antonio in the Texas House of Representatives. During his time in the Legislature, he has risen to become the 10th most senior member of the Texas House of Representatives and the Dean of the Bexar County Delegation. Martinez Fischer previously chaired the House Democratic Caucus, and served as Chair of the Mexican American Legislative Caucus (MALC) from 2009-2016. Rep. Martinez Fischer currently serves as Vice Chair of the House Committee on Ways & Means, and as a member of the House Committee on Culture, Recreation & Tourism. Rep. Martinez Fischer graduated from Oliver Wendell Holmes High School,.",
